{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_7e3a496d41c6b15da5f9cd4761429c801e355372a08a62a370be88a3661481e7"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: development uses Bun (bun install, bun run dev, electron:build, vscode:package), with dev scripts for web HMR, Electron, and VS Code extension development documented in CONTRIBUTING.md."}],"claim_ids":["clm_7e3a496d41c6b15da5f9cd4761429c801e355372a08a62a370be88a3661481e7"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:11:17Z","created_by_operation":"op_a22daabf492e478a84157475254b762f","id":"pg_1f1f157cf98f57ed8a8e69b8f1711345","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/openchamber-openchamber-contributing-md-1636fd2bf8e4-69b8f1711345.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_f0cdfa6e7d4c50ee82c4b36d50749b41"],"title":"openchamber/openchamber/CONTRIBUTING.md @ 1636fd2bf8e4","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:11:17Z","updated_by_operation":"op_a22daabf492e478a84157475254b762f"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_1efe4dedd499521a2fe52f75d95d77a9f926a1019bea6668dfe5d0a3258fcea3"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Session Goals let a user set a finish line; the system checks results after each turn and keeps the agent working until the goal completes, the agent is blocked, or a user-set limit is reached, continuing even after the app is closed."},{"claim_ids":["clm_668da093690b69c89271a2987827b9fe77ed62998975deb44cff48ee2ee34a99"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Remote access pairs devices via a one-time QR code through Private Relay with end-to-end encryption and revocable connections; direct, LAN/VPN, Cloudflare/Ngrok tunnels, and SSH connections are also supported."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6e150bab3f132cd8b409bce5ecfe7c57b5095e48415595db98c8570f40b6aaad"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"OpenChamber uses OpenCode to run coding agents, calling official OpenCode APIs through @opencode-ai/sdk/v2; the CLI/Web and VS Code surfaces use the user's installed OpenCode CLI."},{"claim_ids":["clm_b3b0e08acf4f2370c5aaff4dd5ec63aabc6ce406d45576f6119550c62b144dce"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The CLI exposes commands such as status, connect-url --qr, tunnel start, startup enable, logs, stop, and update, and binds to localhost by default with --lan and --ui-password options."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ba80ba319ebf84f768efca30c786fef102536c92f64ed39c68f69b5512540b4a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Changes Walkthrough turns a large diff into an AI-guided tour that groups related edits into ordered steps and explains how the pieces fit together."},{"claim_ids":["clm_bcb6b6a111ceb495611b5bbc85b345a9000da0d27ac36f5ea81d02ca5390db1c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Multi-run assigns the same task to up to five models in separate sessions with optional worktrees, and Fusion can combine the strongest parts of those runs into a new session."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c18926456ba7136304a277cbaa30f8db247666acc9013e6d313f45920eade665"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The CLI for web/PWA requires Node.js 22+; Linux AppImages require FUSE (libfuse.so.2), with an APPIMAGE_EXTRACT_AND_RUN=1 fallback."}],"claim_ids":["clm_1efe4dedd499521a2fe52f75d95d77a9f926a1019bea6668dfe5d0a3258fcea3","clm_668da093690b69c89271a2987827b9fe77ed62998975deb44cff48ee2ee34a99","clm_6e150bab3f132cd8b409bce5ecfe7c57b5095e48415595db98c8570f40b6aaad","clm_b3b0e08acf4f2370c5aaff4dd5ec63aabc6ce406d45576f6119550c62b144dce","clm_ba80ba319ebf84f768efca30c786fef102536c92f64ed39c68f69b5512540b4a","clm_bcb6b6a111ceb495611b5bbc85b345a9000da0d27ac36f5ea81d02ca5390db1c","clm_c18926456ba7136304a277cbaa30f8db247666acc9013e6d313f45920eade665"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:11:17Z","created_by_operation":"op_a22daabf492e478a84157475254b762f","id":"pg_51e4e2c34a6e5514868633c2cef390c1","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/openchamber-openchamber-readme-md-1636fd2bf8e4-33c2cef390c1.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_751af7928ffa5a4db757b9071dfdfd40"],"title":"openchamber/openchamber/README.md @ 1636fd2bf8e4","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:11:17Z","updated_by_operation":"op_a22daabf492e478a84157475254b762f"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_5495ba05242f8dcb8c464cc80b4d168b5c27f2897691973c04c86526136793b9"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The server exposes WebSocket routes (/api/event/ws, /api/global/event/ws, /api/terminal/ws) and SSE routes (/api/event, /api/global/event, /api/notifications/stream, /api/openchamber/events) that reverse proxies must pass through unbuffered."},{"claim_ids":["clm_78c3e75eb41584e7ab49659c0d6993be4702580e4bfd6708fd319fe5324c6209"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"OpenChamber appears to gzip-compress HTTP responses with a 1 KB threshold while excluding SSE streaming routes from compression, per the reverse-proxy guidance."}],"claim_ids":["clm_5495ba05242f8dcb8c464cc80b4d168b5c27f2897691973c04c86526136793b9","clm_78c3e75eb41584e7ab49659c0d6993be4702580e4bfd6708fd319fe5324c6209"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:11:17Z","created_by_operation":"op_a22daabf492e478a84157475254b762f","id":"pg_705ac381b16556c3a85123cb94f60e58","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/openchamber-openchamber-docs-reverse-proxy-md-1636fd2bf8e4-23cb94f60e58.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_78856a089c08522cb50af67e5392a1b8"],"title":"openchamber/openchamber/docs/REVERSE_PROXY.md @ 1636fd2bf8e4","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:11:17Z","updated_by_operation":"op_a22daabf492e478a84157475254b762f"}
